# Brand Gmail email notification API

POST /api/EmailNotification/Send uses current fixed integration Basic credentials. It is a standalone integration endpoint; it does not automatically connect portal alerts, BIO login, feedback or correspondence workflows to email. The integration credential permits selecting any active brand; BrandID selects its independently enabled sender settings, not a separate caller identity.

## Administrator setup

Apply 001_BrandGmail.sql (Apply.ps1 is local-only), and deploy API/Portal/shared library together. In Modules/Attendance_Integration/ManageAttendanceIntegration.aspx select the brand, then use the Gmail section's separate save button. Enter sender account email, Gmail App Password, and enable email. SMTP is fixed to smtp.gmail.com:465 with implicit TLS (MailKit SslOnConnect); it is not client-selectable. Google documents [SMTP settings](https://support.google.com/mail/answer/7104828?hl=en) and [App Password eligibility and 2-Step Verification](https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/185833?hl=en).

Credentials are DPAPI LocalMachine encrypted using the existing AttendanceIntegration.Protect/Unprotect helper. Portal and API must run on the Windows host that saved the encrypted password; moving them requires re-entering it on the destination. Metadata excludes the password. SQL revalidates the active system administrator before saving or revealing it. Saved values appear masked with the existing eye control, no password ViewState, no-store responses and HTML encoding. Empty edits preserve the saved password; changing the sender requires a new password. Email settings and their rowversion/enable flag are independent from attendance/ERP/BioTime/HR configuration. No credentials are inserted by the migration. Existing PageBase SMTP helpers are not used: they lack this per-brand configuration and are not an API shared service.

## Postman request

Method: POST. URL: REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_SECRETapi/EmailNotification/Send for configured local HTTP development; production should use the environment's HTTPS origin. Transport follows MobileApi.AllowHttp. Authorization: Basic Auth with the existing integration API username/password; this is separate from the selected brand's Gmail account. Do not send Gmail credentials or a From address in the request.

```json
{"BrandID":29,"To":"recipient@example.com","Subject":"رسالة من بروستو","Body":"<div dir=\"rtl\"><h2>مرحبًا</h2><p>نص الرسالة.</p></div>"}
```

BrandID must be positive. To is one bare email address (maximum 254 characters), no display-name/list/header injection. Subject is nonblank, maximum 200 characters with no CR/LF. Body is nonblank HTML, maximum 200,000 characters. JSON names are BrandID, To, Subject, Body only; extra fields are rejected. HTML and subject are UTF-8; no attachment/CC/BCC or SMTP override is supported.

## Responses and retry semantics

200 means SMTP accepted the message, not confirmation that it reached the recipient's inbox:

```json
{"Success":true,"Data":{"BrandID":29,"To":"recipient@example.com","Status":"Submitted"},"Message":"قبل خادم SMTP الرسالة للإرسال؛ وصولها النهائي يعتمد على مزود البريد."}
```

Errors use Success:false and Error:{Code,Message}. They never include the App Password, raw upstream response or message body. Responses are no-store; logs contain only sanitized status/exception types. This endpoint has no idempotency key or automatic retry. On timeouts/network failures, SMTP may already have accepted the message: check before resending. Gmail sender availability, App Password eligibility, rate limits and live delivery must be checked on the intended host/account.

| HTTP | Code | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 400 | INVALID_REQUEST | Body/address/subject validation failed |
| 401 | BASIC_AUTH_REQUIRED / BASIC_AUTH_INVALID | Integration auth missing/incorrect |
| 403 | HTTPS_REQUIRED | Required transport absent |
| 403 | BRAND_UNAVAILABLE | Brand missing/inactive/deleted |
| 403 | EMAIL_DISABLED | Selected brand email is disabled |
| 503 | SMTP_NOT_CONFIGURED | Settings or sender/password absent |
| 503 | SMTP_CONFIG_DECRYPTION_ERROR | Password must be saved on the sending host |
| 503 | EMAIL_CONFIG_UNAVAILABLE | Database settings unavailable |
| 502 | SMTP_AUTH_FAILED | SMTP authentication rejected |
| 502 | SMTP_RECIPIENT_REJECTED | SMTP rejected recipient |
| 502 | SMTP_SEND_FAILED | Other SMTP/provider failure |
| 502 | SMTP_CONNECTION_FAILED | DNS/socket/network connection failed |
| 502 | SMTP_TLS_FAILED | TLS handshake/certificate validation failed |
| 504 | SMTP_TIMEOUT | 30-second send deadline; outcome may be uncertain |
| 500 | EMAIL_SEND_FAILED | Unexpected failure |

## Verification

Test.ps1 uses a disposable SQL fixture, synthetic brand settings, the production authorization/controller pipeline and an injected SMTP capture/failure function. It sends no real email. Coverage includes independent sender selection, DPAPI, metadata secrecy, admin restrictions, rowversion conflicts, preserved passwords, changed-sender requirements, HTML/UTF8, single recipient, header/field validation, disabled/missing brand/settings, transport/Basic and sanitized SMTP errors. A MailKit connection-only probe successfully negotiated Gmail TLS on port 465 from the development host without authentication or sending; live Gmail delivery and authenticated Portal visuals remain unverified. The sender uses MailKit/MimeKit 4.17.0 and their packages.config dependencies for implicit TLS on port 465, retaining the existing injected send function and MailMessage construction. TLS certificates use normal platform validation; no validation bypass or automatic port fallback is enabled. Deploy the API bin dependencies together.

Local validation: Release solution build succeeded; 133 simulated email HTTP/SQL assertions and 198 mobile/BIO assertions passed. ASP.NET precompilation succeeded with generated obj and unrelated historical TestPages excluded. Authenticated visual review and live Gmail delivery remain unverified; no sender credentials were seeded and no email was sent.
